You've already picked the best clover in the patch.	你已經摘走這片草叢裡最好的幸運草了。
The three-leaf clovers are neither interesting nor helpful to you.	三葉草對你來說既沒意思也沒用處。
You can't climb this tree.	你爬不上這棵樹。
Catching the butterfly will not get you any closer to your goal.  And it might hurt the butterfly.	抓蝴蝶不會讓你更接近目標，還可能傷到牠。
Apparently the hot Daventry sun is getting to you.	看來戴凡確王國的烈日曬得你頭昏了。
The butterfly doesn't talk.	蝴蝶不會說話。
This is a charming little yellow butterfly.	這是一隻迷人的小黃蝴蝶。
An unusual clover glistens in the middle of the patch.	草叢中央有一株不尋常的幸運草閃閃發光。
You notice a patch of clover just a few short steps away.	你注意到不遠處有一片幸運草叢。
A jumble of clover grows in this patch of the forest.	森林這片區域雜亂地長著一叢幸運草。
A rough-hewn plank bridge spans the deep rushing river here.	這裡有座粗糙的木板橋，橫跨湍急的深河。
There is no one to talk to here.	這裡沒有人可以交談。
The trees flourish in the moist, healthy soil around the river.	河邊潮濕肥沃的土壤讓樹木長得十分茂盛。
As you start to cross the bridge, a huge, hulking troll stomps into view and blocks your way.  Even though you are invisible, the troll can sense your presence and will not allow you to cross his bridge.	你正要過橋時，一隻魁梧的矮精靈踏著沉重的腳步出現，擋住了你的去路。儘管你隱形著，矮精靈仍能感應到你的存在，不肯讓你過橋。
As you start to cross the bridge, a huge, hulking troll stomps into view and blocks your way.	你正要過橋時，一隻魁梧的矮精靈踏著沉重的腳步出現，擋住了你的去路。
As the troll pushes you back your ring slips off and falls into the river. It's gone forever!	矮精靈把你推了回去，戒指從你手上滑落，掉進河裡。永遠找不回來了！
It is a well known fact that goats hate trolls intensely.  You move aside and let the goat take care of this wretched, nasty troll.	眾所皆知，山羊對矮精靈恨之入骨。你讓到一旁，讓山羊去對付這隻可惡的矮精靈。
The goat lowers his head and runs straight for the troll, butting him right off the bridge and into the river below.  That's the last you'll see of that troll.	山羊低下頭，直直衝向矮精靈，一頭把牠撞下橋、掉進下方的河裡。你再也見不到那隻矮精靈了。
These rocks are worn smooth from countless years of swiftly flowing water.	這些石頭被湍急的流水沖刷了無數年，已經磨得十分光滑。
TROLL: "Well, what've we got here?  You think yer gonna cross my bridge, do you?  Not for FREE, you ain't."	矮精靈：「哼，這是什麼？你以為可以白白過我的橋？沒付錢，休想。」
TROLL: "Yer quite the little chatterbox, aintcha?  Well, lemmee warn ya, these bridges have been in my family for years and years, and nobody, especially not a puny little knight like yerself, has ever passed across one of our bridges without payin' our Troll Toll."	矮精靈：「你話還真多啊？好吧，讓我警告你，這座橋在我家族手裡傳了好幾代，從沒有人，尤其不會是你這種弱不禁風的小騎士，不付『過橋費』就想通過。」
TROLL: "Quit gabbin'.  Are you plannin' on paying my toll, or does I hafta get tough?"	矮精靈：「別廢話了。你到底要不要付過橋費，還是要我對你不客氣？」
A lovely tree overlooks a bend in the river.	一棵美麗的樹俯瞰著河流的轉彎處。
The turbulent river surges over and around the rocks, down the bend to the north.	湍急的河水衝過岩石，往北邊的彎道流去。
This is an attractive meadow.  A particularly large tree stands nearby.	這是一片迷人的草原，附近矗立著一棵特別高大的樹。
They're not ready to leave the nest yet!	牠們還沒準備好離巢！
The birds of Daventry prefer their food untouched by human hands.	戴凡確王國的鳥兒偏好沒被人手碰過的食物。
The mother bird is feeding her young in the nest high above you.	母鳥正在你頭頂高處的鳥巢裡餵食幼鳥。
The baby birds are very hungry.  It will be several weeks before they are able to start feeding themselves.	雛鳥非常餓，還要幾個星期才能自己覓食。
The nest houses a mother bird and her brood of two hungry baby birds.	鳥巢裡住著一隻母鳥和牠兩隻飢餓的雛鳥。
The windows are made from hardened sugar.   You can't see through them very well.	窗戶是用硬化的糖做成的，你看不太清楚裡面。
The candy canes on the window block your view.	窗上的柺杖糖擋住了你的視線。
Mmmmmm! The lovely aroma of baked gingerbread makes your mouth water.	嗯～剛烤好的薑餅香氣四溢，讓你垂涎三尺。
This is the sweetest little gingerbread house you've ever seen.  The walls are cake, the roof is frosting, the chimney is made from gummy bricks, and the candy path and cookie fence are unbearably tempting!	這是你見過最甜美的小薑餅屋。牆壁是蛋糕做的，屋頂是糖霜，煙囪是用軟糖磚砌成的，糖果小徑和餅乾圍籬更是誘人得讓人受不了！
You can't see much from here.	從這裡看不到什麼。
You are near a little gingerbread house in a forest clearing.	你來到森林空地中的一間小薑餅屋附近。
You must be getting nervous! There is no witch anywhere to be seen.	你一定緊張起來了吧！四周根本看不到什麼巫婆。
The path leads to the door.	這條小徑通往大門。
The whole house is made of candy.	整棟房子都是用糖果做的。
It is made of delicious chocolate chip cookies!	這是用美味的巧克力餅乾做成的！
The whole HOUSE is made of gingerbread!	整棟「房子」都是薑餅做的！
The entire ROOF is made of frosting!	整個「屋頂」都是糖霜做的！
Strangely enough, knocking on the door while invisible wouldn't make any sound!	說也奇怪，隱形的時候敲門根本不會發出聲音！
The door is already closed.	門已經關上了。
The windows are too hard to break.	窗戶太硬了，打不破。
You would have to get closer to the windows.	你得靠近窗戶才行。
You don't need to do that; opening the door would suffice.	你不必這麼做，打開門就夠了。
The door is around the corner.	門在轉角那邊。
The door is not locked.	門沒有上鎖。
Yummy!	好好吃！
You will have to move closer to do that.	你得靠近一點才能這麼做。
The gingerbread house with its frosting looks tempting, but you need to get closer.	覆著糖霜的薑餅屋看起來很誘人，但你得靠近一點。
As you begin to eat the house, a squeaky voice from somewhere says, "Nibble, nibble, little mouse.  Who is nibbling at my house?"	你剛開始啃房子，就聽見不知從哪傳來一個尖細的聲音說：「啃啊啃，小老鼠，是誰在啃我的房子？」
Yum! The house tastes even better than it looks!	好吃！這房子嚐起來比看起來還美味！
What candy would you like to eat? The whole house is made of candy.	你想吃哪種糖果？整棟房子都是糖果做的。
The cookies look delicious, but the house looks even better!	餅乾看起來很美味，但房子看起來更棒！
Eat a flower? That seems rather strange.	吃花？這聽起來相當奇怪。
As good as it looks, you're just a little bit suspicious about where all that candy came from.	雖然看起來很美味，你還是有點懷疑這些糖果是從哪來的。
It looks tempting, but you can't reach it from down here.	看起來很誘人，但你在下面搆不到。
You don't know how long they have been standing there.  Eating them probably wouldn't be a wise thing to do.	你不知道它們在那裡放了多久，吃下去恐怕不是明智之舉。
Something...or someone...must be cooking.	一定有什麼……或者什麼人……正在做菜。
The door is made from candy canes.	這扇門是用柺杖糖做成的。
As you knock on the candy cane door, a squeaky voice from inside the house says, "Who is there? I love visitors, especially young, tender ones! Come in, come in!"	你敲了敲柺杖糖做的門，屋裡傳出一個尖細的聲音說：「是誰啊？我最喜歡訪客了，尤其是年輕又嫩的！進來吧，快進來！」
There is no answer from inside the house.	屋裡沒有人回應。
The path to the front door is lined with little gingerbread boys and girls.	通往大門的小徑兩旁排滿了小薑餅男孩和女孩。
Gnarled, ancient trees loom in this dark part of the forest.	這片幽暗的森林裡，矗立著扭曲盤根的古老大樹。
These are some of the largest, plumpest walnuts you have ever seen.	這些是你見過最大、最飽滿的胡桃。
There are some walnuts nearby, under the walnut tree.	胡桃樹下附近散落著幾顆胡桃。
There are no more walnuts to be seen!	已經看不到更多胡桃了！
There is a large walnut tree surrounded by several pine trees.	一棵高大的胡桃樹被幾棵松樹環繞著。
If you've seen one pine tree, you've seen them all.	看過一棵松樹，等於全都看過了。
The tree is loaded with walnuts.	這棵樹上結滿了胡桃。
The walnuts are too hard to see from over here.	從這裡很難看清楚那些胡桃。
Actually, you were quite lucky:  you picked the only gold walnut in the bunch!  The rest are of no use to you.	其實你相當幸運：你摘到的正是這堆裡唯一的金胡桃！其餘的對你都沒有用。
You already have a gold walnut.	你已經有一顆金胡桃了。
Where can you get a gold walnut?	哪裡能找到金胡桃？
You've already picked the only walnut worth getting, though you may not have realized it!	你已經摘走了唯一值得拿的那顆胡桃，只是你可能還沒發現！
You already have one walnut, let's not be greedy.	你已經有一顆胡桃了，別太貪心。
You can't pick it up while you're invisible.	你隱形的時候沒辦法把它撿起來。
It looks like a walnut of some sort.	看起來像是某種胡桃。
What are you throwing at?	你想丟向什麼？
In the manner of a cruel schoolboy, you fling a pebble at the squirrel.  Fortunately, the squirrel is too quick for you.	你像個殘忍的小男孩一樣，朝松鼠丟了一顆鵝卵石。幸好松鼠的動作比你快多了。
You don't have any rocks to throw.	你沒有石頭可以丟。
There is no squirrel here.	這裡沒有松鼠。
The squirrel doesn't want one that you've touched.	松鼠不想要被你碰過的東西。
The squirrel seems hesitant about climbing its favorite walnut tree with you standing around!	你站在旁邊，松鼠似乎不太敢爬上牠最愛的胡桃樹！
There is no squirrel here at the moment.	這裡目前沒有松鼠。
Please don't bother the squirrel, it has a lot of work to do before next winter.	請別打擾松鼠，牠在下一個冬天來臨前還有很多事要忙。
You don't have anything to shoot the squirrel with.	你沒有東西可以拿來射松鼠。
You'll have to have some sort of small, hard projectile in order to use the sling.	你得先有某種小而堅硬的投射物，才能使用投石器。
What would a knight have to gain by murdering such a cute, inoffensive creature as a tiny squirrel?	殺死一隻可愛又無害的小松鼠，對一位騎士能有什麼好處？
It would be cowardly to kill the squirrel, and it would serve no purpose.  Act like a knight!	殺松鼠既懦弱又毫無意義，拿出騎士的樣子來！
The squirrel took the walnut you wanted.	松鼠拿走了你想要的那顆胡桃。
Pick another one instead.	換摘另一顆吧。
There are no more walnuts to pick.	沒有更多胡桃可以摘了。
You'll have to get closer to the nuts.	你得靠近那些胡桃才行。
You choose a big, meaty-looking walnut from the bunch scattered around.	你從散落一地的胡桃中，挑了一顆看起來大又飽滿的。
Naah, you'd get sticky sap and pine needles all over yourself.	算了吧，你會沾得滿身黏答答的樹脂和松針。
They're doing quite nicely where they are, thank you.	它們待在原地好好的，謝了。
There appears to be some sort of bowl sitting next to the tree.	樹旁似乎放著某種碗。
There appears to be some sort of bowl on the ground.	地上似乎放著某種碗。
From what you can see of it, it looks like a colorful bowl of some sort.	從你看到的樣子判斷，這像是某種色彩繽紛的碗。
The ground all around Daventry is carpeted with lush, green grass.	戴凡確王國四周的地面，鋪滿了茂盛翠綠的青草。
A gigantic beanstalk has grown here, stretching up until it disappears into the clouds above.	這裡長出了一株巨大的豆莖，一路向上延伸，直到消失在頭頂的雲層裡。
This is a charming little wooded area of the forest. Pine trees and lush grass grow in the especially rich soil here.	這是森林裡一小片迷人的林地，肥沃的土壤上長滿了松樹和茂密的青草。
Lovely pine trees abound in this forest.	這片森林裡到處都是美麗的松樹。
You've already picked it up.	你已經撿起來了。
You can't pick up the bowl while you're invisible.	你隱形的時候沒辦法撿起那個碗。
You are too busy.	你正忙著呢。
On the far side of the river is a green meadow.	河的對岸是一片綠色草原。
The meadow is on the other side of the river.	草原在河的另一邊。
Water rushes swiftly around the bend and over the rocks.	河水湍急地繞過彎道、越過岩石。
You see a lovely green meadow on the other side of the river.	你看見河的另一邊有片美麗的綠色草原。
The swiftly-moving water is even more dangerous than it looks.	湍急的河水比看起來還要危險。
The meadow is on the other side of the raging river.	草原在這條洶湧河流的另一邊。
Around the rugged rocks the reckless river rages.	洶湧的河水在崎嶇的岩石間肆虐奔騰。
High cliffs border a wild, raging river.	高聳的懸崖夾著一條狂野洶湧的河流。
You notice an enchanting meadow.	你注意到一片迷人的草原。
The meadow on the other side of the river looks very peaceful and enchanting.	河對岸的草原看起來十分寧靜迷人。
Some of the rocks poke up from the riverbed.  These rocks are actually very tall and treacherous!	河床上突出幾塊岩石，這些岩石其實又高又危險！
No way.  Who knows what squirmy, slimy creatures are lurking underneath?	才不要。誰知道底下潛伏著什麼扭來扭去的黏滑生物？
There are craggy rocks scattered around the forest. You hate to think of what's underneath them.	森林四處散落著崎嶇的岩石，你不敢去想岩石底下藏著什麼。
You are in an eerie, desolate part of the forest.	你來到森林裡一處陰森荒涼的地方。
The trees are bent and stunted, making the forest look even gloomier.	樹木彎曲又發育不良，讓森林看起來更加陰森。
There's nothing to be gained by reaching into the hole.	把手伸進洞裡不會有任何收穫。
You would need to be much smaller to fit through that hole.	你得小上許多，才能穿過那個洞。
You might just as well try to hold a moonbeam in your hand!	你不如試試用手抓住一道月光算了！
This rock is firmly stuck in the ground.	這塊石頭牢牢卡在地上。
Although you are very strong and healthy, this rock is too much even for you.	雖然你身強體健，這塊石頭還是太重，連你也搬不動。
The hole appears to go deep down through the rock, into the ground below.  You can barely make out a faint greenish glow somewhere far inside.	這個洞似乎深深穿透岩石，通往地底深處。你隱約能看見遠方深處有一絲微弱的綠光。
